From: Haldexx
Subject: [PATCH] ptrace: do not clear the event message in ptrace_check_attach()

The donor kernel's ptrace_check_attach() starts by zeroing
child->ptrace_message. Every ptrace request passes through it before it
is dispatched, so PTRACE_GETEVENTMSG always returned 0: the new pid of a
PTRACE_EVENT_CLONE/FORK/VFORK, the exit status of PTRACE_EVENT_EXIT and
the seccomp data were all lost. Upstream 3.10 has no such line.

On Android 16 this disables every tombstone. crash_dump follows the
crashing process's double clone of its snapshot process with
PTRACE_O_TRACECLONE, reads pid 0, fails in waitpid(0) ("failed to waitpid
on child: No child processes") and exits 1. Measured on the SM-N920I with
a freestanding test: PTRACE_GETEVENTMSG after PTRACE_EVENT_CLONE and
PTRACE_EVENT_FORK returned msg=0 while the child pids were 12186/12188.

---
diff --git a/kernel/ptrace.c b/kernel/ptrace.c
index aa469af2..e518b3ac 100644
--- a/kernel/ptrace.c
+++ b/kernel/ptrace.c
@@ -185,7 +185,6 @@ static void ptrace_unfreeze_traced(struct task_struct *task)
 static int ptrace_check_attach(struct task_struct *child, bool ignore_state)
 {
 	int ret = -ESRCH;
-	child->ptrace_message = 0;
 
 	/*
 	 * We take the read lock around doing both checks to close a
